Description: preview-driven Qt frontend for rsync
 qt-rsync compares a Source and a Destination with an rsync dry run and
 shows the differences in three synchronized comparison panes plus an
 overview. Files are written only after the selected decisions have been
 reviewed in the synchronization confirmation dialog.
 .
 The application is a pure Qt 6 / C++ port of qpy-rsync. Decisions,
 execution plans, filters and the comparison data live in one C++ core;
 there is no Python runtime. The journal records every command before it
 runs, transfers can be cancelled or paused, and profiles can be stored for
 recurring jobs.
